Description: Audible notifications for system service state changes
 Sparky Beep provides audible notifications (beeps) when selected system
 services start, stop, or restart. It was made for the SparkyLinux Server
 Edition and uses the PC speaker to create distinctive sound patterns for
 different service state changes.
 .
 Features:
  * Service-specific beep patterns for SSH, Samba, NetData, and Webmin
  * TUI and GUI configuration interfaces for easy setup
  * Multi-language support (26 languages)
  * Custom tune library with 10+ built-in melodies
  * Time-based scheduling with quiet hours support
  * Musical composition system for creating custom beep sequences
  * Automatic service discovery and management
 .
 The beep services bind to the watched systemd units, so the PC speaker
 reports their state changes. The ternary engine (tbeep) uses x86 port I/O,
 so the package is built for amd64 and i386.
